---
import Todo from '@/components/ui/Todo.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import IndustryLayout from '@/layouts/IndustryLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Do you make suspension or valve springs?',
    a: 'No. Those use wire above our 2.50 mm limit. Work in our unit is light: detents, returns, clips and small seat or lock springs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you make two-wheeler springs?',
    a: 'Two-wheeler assemblies often use torsion and extension springs in this wire range. Whether that is a regular RK product is still to be confirmed.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the minimum order?',
    a: `Usually ${site.terms.moq}. Smaller development runs are charged. We quote within 24 hours.`,
  },
];
---

<IndustryLayout
  route="automotive"
  title="Automotive Springs, Pune"
  description="Light automotive springs and wire forms, wire Ø 0.40–2.50 mm. Detents, returns and clips to drawing or sample. Not suspension coils."
  h1="Automotive springs"
  lede="Light springs for vehicle assemblies, in the 0.40–2.50 mm wire range. Not coil springs for suspension, and not heavy valve springs."
  context="automotive springs"
  faqs={faqs}
  related={[
    { to: 'torsion', label: 'Torsion springs', description: 'The largest share of what we coil.' },
    { to: 'wireForms', label: 'Wire forms', description: 'Clips, hooks and pins.' },
    {
      to: 'switchgear',
      label: 'Electrical and switchgear',
      description: 'MCB and switch mechanisms.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <h2>What we can make for a vehicle</h2>
  <p>
    Automobile is one of the industries we serve. In our wire range that usually means a{' '}
    <strong>detent, a return, a small seat spring or a clip</strong> — not a suspension coil and not
    a heavy engine valve spring.
  </p>
  <p>
    Torsion and double torsion springs turn up in levers and locks. Extension springs turn up in
    returns. Compression springs sit under buttons and in small valves. Wire forms become clips and
    pins.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two-wheeler work is a common use of these types.
    <Todo text="confirm whether two-wheeler springs are a regular RK product, before we treat it as one." />
  </p>

  <h2>What the drawing must say</h2>
  <p>
    Oil, heat, outdoor parking and road dirt decide the material. Hard-drawn spring steel is fine
    when the part stays dry. Stainless 302 / 304 is the usual step up if rust would jam the
    mechanism. Tell us the finish if the part is visible or if the buyer spec names one. Plating
    goes through partners.
  </p>
  <p>
    The unit is ZED certified. A development sample goes into your assembly before we run the bulk
    quantity.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    Wire {site.capability.wireRangeLabel}. Usual minimum {site.terms.moq}. Quote within 24 hours.
    Dispatch is ex-works Talawade. We supply across India; we do not export.
  </p>
</IndustryLayout>
